rules can be added. The resulting music
follows the given harmony, but the pitch
sequence also (tries to) follow the pitch
sequence of the selected voice. 
An additional instance of follow-profile-hr
ensures that also the rhythm of the
selected voice is followed.
Note that heuristic rules do not cause any
search, i.e., the solver does not necessarily
find the best possible solution. The solver
always chooses first the pitches of the
given voice or close pitches, but it never
backtracks to find a better solution. For
example, if you select to constrain only the
intervals instead of the profile, then the
solver will not try to find the best starting
value that results in the closes match.
Nevertheless, heuristics can have a strong
influence on the solution. " (om-make-point 271 347) (quote "This example demonstrates how additional$rules can be added. The resulting music$follows the given harmony, but the pitch$sequence also (tries to) follow the pitch$sequence of the selected voice. $$An additional instance of follow-profile-hr$ensures that also the rhythm of the$selected voice is followed.$$Note that heuristic rules do not cause any$search, i.e., the solver does not necessarily$find the best possible solution. The solver$always chooses first the pitches of the$given voice or close pitches, but it never$backtracks to find a better solution. For$example, if you select to constrain only the$intervals instead of the profile, then the$solver will not try to find the best starting$value that results in the closes match.$Nevertheless, heuristics can have a strong$influence on the solution. ") "" (om-make-point 910 183) nil (om-make-color 0 0 0) (om-make-font "Verdana" 12 :family "Verdana" :style (quote (:plain)) :mode (quote nil))))) (when (fboundp (quote set-active)) (set-active box nil)) box))) (quote ((4 0 0 0 nil 0) (13 0 1 0 nil 0) (2 0 3 0 nil 0) (5 0 4 0 nil 0) (3 0 4 1 nil 0) (0 0 6 0 nil 0) (6 0 7 0 nil 0) (9 0 8 0 nil 0) (13 0 10 0 nil 0) (13 0 11 0 nil 0) (13 0 12 0 nil 0) (10 0 14 0 nil 0) (11 0 14 1 nil 0) (12 0 14 2 nil 0) (1 0 14 3 nil 0) (7 0 21 0 nil 0) (8 0 21 1 nil 0) (14 0 21 2 nil 0) (21 0 22 3 nil 0) (17 0 22 7 nil 0) (18 0 22 8 nil 0) (19 0 22 9 nil 0) (20 0 22 10 nil 0) (15 0 22 11 nil 0) (16 0 22 12 nil 0) (22 0 23 1 nil 0))) nil 8.0))